WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.513 --> 00:00:15.417
After Zann left, Fala went back upstairs.

2
00:00:16.318 --> 00:00:18.158
Teplo busied himself reading some papers.

3
00:00:18.859 --> 00:00:23.941
Perda finished the food Fala had conjured and looked around, feeling restless and worried about Zann.

4
00:00:23.961 --> 00:00:27.662
"I wish we could do something useful," she told Darb.

5
00:00:27.682 --> 00:00:29.643
"I hate just sitting here."

6
00:00:30.644 --> 00:00:31.464
Darb didn't answer.

7
00:00:31.808 --> 00:00:33.229
He was staring into space.

8
00:00:34.090 --> 00:00:35.310
Perda poked him in the arm.

9
00:00:35.330 --> 00:00:36.611
"Huh?" he said.

10
00:00:36.631 --> 00:00:37.752
"Oh, sorry.

11
00:00:38.433 --> 00:00:39.713
I was just thinking about Zing.

12
00:00:40.114 --> 00:00:40.914
I hope he's okay."

13
00:00:40.934 --> 00:00:43.476
"I'm sure he's fine," Perda said.

14
00:00:43.496 --> 00:00:45.998
"I wish we could get him back though."

15
00:00:47.018 --> 00:00:47.859
Teplo looked over.

16
00:00:47.879 --> 00:00:49.800
"Who are you talking about?"

17
00:00:49.820 --> 00:00:52.842
"Zann's pet dragon," Perda said.

18
00:00:52.862 --> 00:00:58.166
"Remember? We told you the palace people took him away when he tried to burn down the door."

19
00:00:58.906 --> 00:01:00.007
Teplo's face lit up.

20
00:01:00.467 --> 00:01:01.408
"I think I can help."

21
00:01:02.216 --> 00:01:03.457
He let out a sharp whistle.

22
00:01:04.158 --> 00:01:07.701
A moment later they heard a rustle of feathers from a dark corner of the room.

23
00:01:08.442 --> 00:01:11.245
Then a large waterfowl waddled into view.

24
00:01:12.326 --> 00:01:12.966
"What's that?"

25
00:01:13.327 --> 00:01:14.748
Darb took a step toward the creature.

26
00:01:14.768 --> 00:01:18.071
"Careful," Teplo said as the bird snapped at Darb.

27
00:01:18.091 --> 00:01:20.233
"She's rather foul-tempered.

28
00:01:20.553 --> 00:01:21.594
She's a sniffer goose."

29
00:01:22.395 --> 00:01:22.855
"A what?"

30
00:01:23.176 --> 00:01:24.157
Darb looked confused.

31
00:01:24.477 --> 00:01:25.938
"I've never heard of that species.

32
00:01:26.639 --> 00:01:27.420
Where do they come from?"

33
00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:33.481
"A sniffer goose is a creature whose entire purpose is tracking dragons," Teplo said.

34
00:01:33.501 --> 00:01:37.823
"If you describe Zann's dragon, she should be able to retrieve him."

35
00:01:38.463 --> 00:01:43.364
Perda noticed that the old man hadn't answered Darb's question about where the sniffer goose was from.

36
00:01:44.004 --> 00:01:45.024
But she didn't really care.

37
00:01:45.465 --> 00:01:47.705
If they could get Zing back, Zann would be thrilled.

38
00:01:47.725 --> 00:01:50.686
"Zing's a fire whistler," she said.

39
00:01:50.706 --> 00:01:54.347
"He's kind of small, with reddish-bronze scales."

40
00:01:55.227 --> 00:01:58.028
She and Darb went on to describe Zing as well as they could.

41
00:01:59.052 --> 00:02:03.914
Teplo listened and translated their description into a series of whistles, grunts, and clicks.

42
00:02:04.614 --> 00:02:06.175
The goose tilted her head and listened.

43
00:02:06.195 --> 00:02:08.716
"You speak this bird's language?"

44
00:02:09.016 --> 00:02:10.417
Darb asked, looking impressed.

45
00:02:10.437 --> 00:02:13.498
"I speak sniffer goose well enough to get by."

46
00:02:13.878 --> 00:02:14.539
Teplo shrugged.

47
00:02:14.559 --> 00:02:16.800
"It's an easy language to learn.

48
00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:21.622
It's even simpler than Troll, and just about anyone can learn that with little trouble."

49
00:02:22.662 --> 00:02:23.663
"If you say so."

50
00:02:23.983 --> 00:02:25.063
Perda watched the bird.

51
00:02:25.083 --> 00:02:26.744
"Now what happens?"

52
00:02:27.712 --> 00:02:29.273
"Go, my feathered friend!"

53
00:02:29.693 --> 00:02:32.615
Teplo fluttered his hands at the goose and let out a honk.

54
00:02:33.095 --> 00:02:36.137
The sniffer goose honked loudly in reply and flapped her wings.

55
00:02:36.857 --> 00:02:39.258
Teplo pulled on a lever, opening the trapdoor.

56
00:02:39.939 --> 00:02:42.480
Honking eagerly, the goose flew up and out.

57
00:02:44.301 --> 00:02:46.582
Teplo closed the trapdoor and smiled at the kids.

58
00:02:46.602 --> 00:02:47.763
"Now we wait."

59
00:02:47.783 --> 00:02:50.664
"Who are you?"

60
00:02:51.104 --> 00:02:54.086
Zann asked as he floated along behind the mysterious people.

61
00:02:54.987 --> 00:02:56.087
"Where are you taking me?"

62
00:02:56.107 --> 00:03:00.445
"Hurry." One of the people shoved Zann's bubble through a doorway.

63
00:03:01.286 --> 00:03:07.109
The bubble touched down and faded, and Zann found himself in a windowless room, face to face with

64
00:03:07.189 --> 00:03:09.611
Yog. Zann gasped.

65
00:03:09.911 --> 00:03:11.912
"Did you come to take me back to the palace?"

66
00:03:12.612 --> 00:03:13.813
Yog grinned at him.

67
00:03:13.833 --> 00:03:14.873
"Not exactly.

68
00:03:15.434 --> 00:03:18.756
But you should have seen Rixa's face when she found out that you four were gone!"

69
00:03:19.516 --> 00:03:20.537
Zann was confused.

70
00:03:21.237 --> 00:03:23.899
He glanced at the others, but he didn't recognize any of them.

71
00:03:25.539 --> 00:03:28.341
"Then why—" "Zann!"

72
00:03:28.721 --> 00:03:29.921
a woman's voice interrupted.

73
00:03:29.941 --> 00:03:31.762
"It's a pleasure to meet you."

74
00:03:32.583 --> 00:03:33.563
Zann turned around.

75
00:03:34.264 --> 00:03:36.445
A tall, imposing woman had just entered.

76
00:03:36.465 --> 00:03:38.806
"This is Venna," Yog said.

77
00:03:38.826 --> 00:03:41.988
"She's one of the few remaining free members of the Red Council."

78
00:03:42.668 --> 00:03:47.051
Zann had heard of Venna, one of the strongest Magic Masters of her generation.

79
00:03:47.071 --> 00:03:49.652
"Nice to meet you too," he said.

80
00:03:49.672 --> 00:03:54.475
"Sorry we had to grab you off the street like that, Zann," Venna said.

81
00:03:54.495 --> 00:03:56.896
"But it's not safe for you out there.

82
00:03:57.612 --> 00:04:01.554
When I got Teplo's message, I immediately sent my associates to fetch you.

83
00:04:02.355 --> 00:04:06.057
On their way they spotted you and decided to intercept you before the trolls did."

84
00:04:06.077 --> 00:04:08.898
"I was fine," Zann protested.

85
00:04:08.918 --> 00:04:11.480
"Indeed," Venna said.

86
00:04:11.500 --> 00:04:15.062
"I'm thrilled that you've eluded the trolls this long.

87
00:04:15.742 --> 00:04:18.824
You must be just as talented as Boz and your parents."

88
00:04:19.725 --> 00:04:20.365
"My parents?"

89
00:04:20.785 --> 00:04:21.305
Zann said.

90
00:04:21.325 --> 00:04:23.707
"Do—did you know them?"

91
00:04:23.727 --> 00:04:25.328
"Of course!

92
00:04:25.964 --> 00:04:31.368
Everyone in First City knew of their fascinating research and mourned the loss of their genius."

93
00:04:32.528 --> 00:04:34.129
Zann wasn't sure what to say to that.

94
00:04:34.950 --> 00:04:37.752
Luckily Venna didn't seem to expect him to say anything.

95
00:04:37.772 --> 00:04:42.155
"That's why I'm so confident you're the right choice," she said.

96
00:04:42.175 --> 00:04:44.556
"The right choice for what?"

97
00:04:45.017 --> 00:04:45.577
Zann asked.

98
00:04:46.277 --> 00:04:46.978
Venna smiled.

99
00:04:46.998 --> 00:04:49.880
"To become the next king of Magica."

100
00:04:57.760 --> 00:04:58.481
"What do you want?"

101
00:04:58.861 --> 00:05:00.842
Morb snapped at the troll who had just entered.

102
00:05:00.862 --> 00:05:03.204
"Can't you see that I'm busy?"

103
00:05:03.964 --> 00:05:05.445
The troll didn't respond for a moment.

104
00:05:06.086 --> 00:05:09.588
It stared at Morb's new contraption, fear in its dull eyes.

105
00:05:09.608 --> 00:05:12.650
"Well?" Morb said impatiently.

106
00:05:13.330 --> 00:05:15.552
The troll finally looked at him and let out a grunt.

107
00:05:16.533 --> 00:05:19.454
An image formed briefly above its head and then sputtered out.

108
00:05:20.255 --> 00:05:21.076
Morb frowned.

109
00:05:21.096 --> 00:05:24.338
"Was that the boy—Boz's grandson?"

110
00:05:24.738 --> 00:05:25.298
he demanded.

111
00:05:25.318 --> 00:05:27.560
"Did you idiots finally capture him?"

112
00:05:28.436 --> 00:05:29.517
The troll shook its head.

113
00:05:30.257 --> 00:05:34.100
Another puff of magical energy showed Zann with a crown on his head.

114
00:05:34.120 --> 00:05:36.901
"What?" Morb exclaimed.

115
00:05:36.921 --> 00:05:38.803
"They're making him king?

116
00:05:39.343 --> 00:05:43.946
Impossible!" The troll grunted, but Morb had never bothered to learn its language.

117
00:05:44.766 --> 00:05:48.989
Morb was tempted to stop what he was doing to find out more but he decided against it.

118
00:05:49.789 --> 00:05:50.730
Soon it wouldn't matter.

119
00:05:51.490 --> 00:05:53.592
Morb looked at his contraption with satisfaction.

120
00:05:54.304 --> 00:05:58.447
The pythons the old woman had brought were writhing in a large glass tube in the middle.

121
00:05:59.467 --> 00:06:03.090
The bone-and-wire frame filled most of the space in the underground room.

122
00:06:03.950 --> 00:06:09.534
Soon, very soon now, it would be time to move it to a larger location, and Morb had

123
00:06:09.554 --> 00:06:10.935
a particular spot in mind.

124
00:06:11.695 --> 00:06:13.876
There Morb would have more space to work.

125
00:06:14.617 --> 00:06:18.199
There he would be able to find the few remaining parts he needed.
